IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `jt69-nouns`
IMPORT `jt69-cross-references`

-- Row il-69. TESTS THAT PIN THE READINGS of the two items: the words of the paragraph as first enacted, the string the instruction replaces, the words it puts in place, what replacing gives, what the consolidation prints, the status of each provision, both limbs, how each was read, and the flags.
-- These pass: they say what was read from what. The assertions that fail on purpose are in jt69-tests-red.l4.
-- The expected values are hand-written from NOTES.md section 6 (the answer tables) and from the quotation strings; the two long lists below were put together by a script from the quotation strings, not from the references module.
-- Nothing here says which reading of paragraph (4) is the right one: the tests state what each text prints.

§ `Tests of the readings`

-- I1: the paragraph as first enacted (the page image), word by word.
#ASSERT `item I1: the paragraph as first enacted`'s `its words` EQUALS LIST "כיהן", "כדירקטור", "או", "מינה", "דירקטור", "או", "מילא", "תפקיד", "או", "העסיק", "אדם", "בניגוד", "להוראות", "סעיף", "23(ב)"
#ASSERT count (`item I1: the paragraph as first enacted`'s `its words`) EQUALS 15
-- The last word of the paragraph is the string the instruction replaces, and the word before it is the word for "section".
#ASSERT at (`item I1: the paragraph as first enacted`'s `its words`) 14 EQUALS `item I1: the instruction of 2011`'s `the string it replaces`
#ASSERT at (`item I1: the paragraph as first enacted`'s `its words`) 13 EQUALS "סעיף"
-- The instruction: the string it replaces and the words it puts in place.
#ASSERT `item I1: the instruction of 2011`'s `the string it replaces` EQUALS "23(ב)"
#ASSERT `item I1: the instruction of 2011`'s `the words it puts in place` EQUALS LIST "לאחר", "שהרשות", "השעתה", "אותו", "מתפקידו", "לפי", "סעיף", "23(א)"
#ASSERT count (`item I1: the instruction of 2011`'s `the words it puts in place`) EQUALS 8

-- I1: the literal result of replacing the string by the words, as the instruction is written.
#ASSERT `the literal result of the instruction` `item I1: section 124(a)(4) cites section 23(b)` EQUALS LIST "כיהן", "כדירקטור", "או", "מינה", "דירקטור", "או", "מילא", "תפקיד", "או", "העסיק", "אדם", "בניגוד", "להוראות", "סעיף", "לאחר", "שהרשות", "השעתה", "אותו", "מתפקידו", "לפי", "סעיף", "23(א)"
#ASSERT count (`the literal result of the instruction` `item I1: section 124(a)(4) cites section 23(b)`) EQUALS 22
-- I1: the consolidation prints the first-enacted words followed by the replacement words (the old citation kept).
#ASSERT `item I1: the consolidation text`'s `its words` EQUALS LIST "כיהן", "כדירקטור", "או", "מינה", "דירקטור", "או", "מילא", "תפקיד", "או", "העסיק", "אדם", "בניגוד", "להוראות", "סעיף", "23(ב)", "לאחר", "שהרשות", "השעתה", "אותו", "מתפקידו", "לפי", "סעיף", "23(א)"
#ASSERT `item I1: the consolidation text`'s `its words` EQUALS append (`item I1: the paragraph as first enacted`'s `its words`) (`item I1: the instruction of 2011`'s `the words it puts in place`)
#ASSERT count (`item I1: the consolidation text`'s `its words`) EQUALS 23
-- The two texts are different lists of words.
#ASSERT NOT (`the literal result of the instruction` `item I1: section 124(a)(4) cites section 23(b)` EQUALS `item I1: the consolidation text`'s `its words`)

-- I1: the one question, asked of each text: is every occurrence of the word for "section" followed by a section number? The first-enacted words and the consolidation's words pass it; the literal result is the one that does not (that assertion is in jt69-tests-red.l4).
#ASSERT `every occurrence of the word is followed by a section number` "סעיף" (`item I1: the paragraph as first enacted`'s `its words`)
#ASSERT `every occurrence of the word is followed by a section number` "סעיף" (`item I1: the consolidation text`'s `its words`)
-- What follows each occurrence of the word for "section" in the literal result: the first replacement word, then the citation of subsection (a).
#ASSERT `the words that follow the word` "סעיף" (`the literal result of the instruction` `item I1: section 124(a)(4) cites section 23(b)`) EQUALS LIST "לאחר", "23(א)"
-- The provisions the three texts cite, among those in the table.
#ASSERT map (GIVEN p YIELD p's `its label`) (`the provisions the words cite` "סעיף" (`item I1: the paragraph as first enacted`'s `its words`) `the provisions item I1 can cite`) EQUALS LIST "section 23(b)"
#ASSERT map (GIVEN p YIELD p's `its label`) (`the provisions the words cite` "סעיף" (`the literal result of the instruction` `item I1: section 124(a)(4) cites section 23(b)`) `the provisions item I1 can cite`) EQUALS LIST "section 23(a)"
#ASSERT map (GIVEN p YIELD p's `its label`) (`the provisions the words cite` "סעיף" (`item I1: the consolidation text`'s `its words`) `the provisions item I1 can cite`) EQUALS LIST "section 23(b)", "section 23(a)"
#ASSERT `the words cite no repealed provision` "סעיף" (`the literal result of the instruction` `item I1: section 124(a)(4) cites section 23(b)`) `the provisions item I1 can cite`
#ASSERT `the words cite no repealed provision` "סעיף" (`item I1: the paragraph as first enacted`'s `its words`) `the provisions item I1 can cite` EQUALS FALSE

-- The status of each provision, as the instruments read give it.
#ASSERT `section 23(b)`'s `its status in the instruments read` EQUALS Repealed
#ASSERT `section 23(a)`'s `its status in the instruments read` EQUALS `Amended and in force`
#ASSERT `section 41`'s `its status in the instruments read` EQUALS Repealed
#ASSERT `section 42`'s `its status in the instruments read` EQUALS `In force`

-- The printed date of the instrument that changes each provision is the date its issue's footer prints; nothing here is a day of effect.
#ASSERT `section 23(b)`'s `the printed date of that instrument` EQUALS JUST (Date 27 1 2011)
#ASSERT `section 23(a)`'s `the printed date of that instrument` EQUALS JUST (Date 27 1 2011)
#ASSERT `section 41`'s `the printed date of that instrument` EQUALS JUST (Date 15 6 2010)
#ASSERT `section 42`'s `the printed date of that instrument` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the day the change to the provision took effect` `section 23(b)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the day the change to the provision took effect` `section 41` EQUALS NOTHING

-- I2: the number the citing words name, and the section value they reach.
#ASSERT `item I2: section 113d(a)(1) cites section 41`'s `the number of the section cited` EQUALS 41
#ASSERT `item I2: section 113d(a)(1) cites section 41`'s `the section cited`'s `its section number` EQUALS 41
#ASSERT `item I2: section 113d(a)(1) cites section 41`'s `the number of the section cited` EQUALS `repeal of section 41 by SH 2243 section 9`'s `the section repealed`
#ASSERT `control to I2: section 113d(a)(2) cites section 42`'s `the section cited`'s `its section number` EQUALS 42

-- I2: the commencement clause as two alternatives, each a period and the date printed on the instrument it runs from. The later of the two is not computed.
#ASSERT map (GIVEN a YIELD a's `the number of months`) (`repeal of section 41 by SH 2243 section 9`'s `the alternatives the clause names`) EQUALS LIST 3, 6
#ASSERT map (GIVEN a YIELD a's `counted from the date printed on`) (`repeal of section 41 by SH 2243 section 9`'s `the alternatives the clause names`) EQUALS LIST (Date 15 6 2010), (Date 26 11 2014)
#ASSERT `repeal of section 41 by SH 2243 section 9`'s `the clause takes the later of the alternatives`
#ASSERT `repeal of section 41 by SH 2243 section 9`'s `the later alternative as a date` EQUALS NOTHING
-- I2: the upper bound, a bound and not a commencement date, and the arithmetic that stands behind it: the bound is 401 days after 26.11.2014 (computed outside L4), which is more than a year after it, and six months is less than a year however the months are counted.
#ASSERT `repeal of section 41 by SH 2243 section 9`'s `an upper bound on the day the repeal began, not a commencement date` EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 2016)
#ASSERT Day (Date 1 1 2016) - Day (Date 26 11 2014) EQUALS 401
#ASSERT `the bound is later than a year after the printed date of every alternative` `repeal of section 41 by SH 2243 section 9`
-- I2: in force on a day, as the instruments read give it. Settled (not in force) only for a day later than the bound; NOTHING for a day that is not.
#ASSERT `the provision is in force on` `section 41` (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the provision is in force on` `section 41` (Date 1 1 2016) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the provision is in force on` `section 41` (Date 1 1 2015) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the provision is in force on` `section 23(b)` (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the provision is in force on` `section 42` (Date 1 1 2015) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Both limbs hold for the two items; the control's limb (a) is false on purpose (its target is not repealed on the instruments read).
#ASSERT `both limbs of the replacement item hold` `item I1: section 124(a)(4) cites section 23(b)`
#ASSERT `both limbs of the reference hold` `item I2: section 113d(a)(1) cites section 41`
#ASSERT `control to I2: section 113d(a)(2) cites section 42`'s `limb (a) holds` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `control to I2: section 113d(a)(2) cites section 42`'s `limb (b) holds`
#ASSERT NOT (`both limbs of the reference hold` `control to I2: section 113d(a)(2) cites section 42`)

-- How each limb was read.
#ASSERT `item I1: section 124(a)(4) cites section 23(b)`'s `limb (a) was read` EQUALS `official page image`
#ASSERT `item I1: section 124(a)(4) cites section 23(b)`'s `limb (b) was read` EQUALS `official page images, with the later instruments read and deposited (see NOTES.md)`
#ASSERT `item I2: section 113d(a)(1) cites section 41`'s `limb (a) was read` EQUALS `official page image`
#ASSERT `item I2: section 113d(a)(1) cites section 41`'s `limb (b) was read` EQUALS `official page images, with the later instruments read and deposited (see NOTES.md)`

-- Limb (b), item I1: the instruments read after the 2011 instruction. Each is printed after it, each names the Joint Investment Trusts Law, and the only paragraph of the Law each names is paragraph (18) of section 124(a), not paragraph (4).
#ASSERT map (GIVEN i YIELD i's `where it is printed`) (`item I1: section 124(a)(4) cites section 23(b)`'s `the later instruments read`) EQUALS LIST "SH 3232 printed page 991, item 14", "SH 3579 printed page 1071, item 3, paragraph (11)"
#ASSERT concat (map (GIVEN i YIELD i's `the paragraphs of the Law it names`) (`item I1: section 124(a)(4) cites section 23(b)`'s `the later instruments read`)) EQUALS LIST "124(a)(18)", "124(a)(18)"
#ASSERT all (GIVEN i YIELD `the instrument is printed after` i (Date 27 1 2011)) (`item I1: section 124(a)(4) cites section 23(b)`'s `the later instruments read`)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN i YIELD i's `the law the issue names for the item` EQUALS "Joint Investment Trusts Law, 5754-1994") (`item I1: section 124(a)(4) cites section 23(b)`'s `the later instruments read`)
#ASSERT `item I1: section 124(a)(4) cites section 23(b)`'s `the paragraph the item records` EQUALS "124(a)(4)"
#ASSERT NOT (`a later instrument read touches the paragraph of the item` `item I1: section 124(a)(4) cites section 23(b)`)

-- Limb (b), item I2 and its control: the instruments read after the issue that prints the citing words. Each is printed after it and names the Joint Investment Trusts Law; none names paragraph (1) or paragraph (2) of subsection (a) of section 113d.
#ASSERT map (GIVEN i YIELD i's `where it is printed`) (`item I2: section 113d(a)(1) cites section 41`'s `the later instruments read`) EQUALS LIST "SH 2654 printed page 1069, item 27", "SH 3232 printed page 991, item 13", "SH 3579 printed page 1071, item 3, paragraph (10)"
#ASSERT concat (map (GIVEN i YIELD i's `the paragraphs of the Law it names`) (`item I2: section 113d(a)(1) cites section 41`'s `the later instruments read`)) EQUALS LIST "113d(b)(1)", "113d(a)(6)", "113d(b)(3)", "113d(a)(6)", "113d(b)(3)"
#ASSERT all (GIVEN i YIELD `the instrument is printed after` i (Date 30 7 2014)) (`item I2: section 113d(a)(1) cites section 41`'s `the later instruments read`)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN i YIELD i's `the law the issue names for the item` EQUALS "Joint Investment Trusts Law, 5754-1994") (`item I2: section 113d(a)(1) cites section 41`'s `the later instruments read`)
#ASSERT `item I2: section 113d(a)(1) cites section 41`'s `the paragraph the reference records` EQUALS "113d(a)(1)"
#ASSERT NOT (`a later instrument read touches the paragraph of the reference` `item I2: section 113d(a)(1) cites section 41`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a later instrument read touches the paragraph of the reference` `control to I2: section 113d(a)(2) cites section 42`)
#ASSERT `control to I2: section 113d(a)(2) cites section 42`'s `the later instruments read` EQUALS `item I2: section 113d(a)(1) cites section 41`'s `the later instruments read`
-- What each later instrument does and the issue date its footer prints.
#ASSERT `SH 2654 item 27`'s `the paragraphs of the Law it names` EQUALS LIST "113d(b)(1)"
#ASSERT `the instrument names the paragraph` "113d(b)(1)" `SH 2654 item 27`
#ASSERT NOT (`the instrument names the paragraph` "113d(a)(1)" `SH 2654 item 27`)
#ASSERT `SH 2654 item 27`'s `what the item does` EQUALS "deletes words from paragraph (1) of subsection (b) of section 113d"
#ASSERT `SH 3232 item 13`'s `the paragraphs of the Law it names` EQUALS LIST "113d(a)(6)", "113d(b)(3)"
#ASSERT `SH 3579 item 3 paragraph (10)`'s `the paragraphs of the Law it names` EQUALS LIST "113d(a)(6)", "113d(b)(3)"
#ASSERT `SH 3232 item 14`'s `the paragraphs of the Law it names` EQUALS LIST "124(a)(18)"
#ASSERT `SH 3579 item 3 paragraph (11)`'s `the paragraphs of the Law it names` EQUALS LIST "124(a)(18)"
#ASSERT `SH 2654 item 27`'s `the printed date of the issue` EQUALS (Date 3 8 2017)
#ASSERT `SH 3232 item 13`'s `the printed date of the issue` EQUALS (Date 3 7 2024)
#ASSERT `SH 3232 item 14`'s `the printed date of the issue` EQUALS (Date 3 7 2024)
#ASSERT `SH 3579 item 3 paragraph (10)`'s `the printed date of the issue` EQUALS (Date 2 8 2026)
#ASSERT `SH 3579 item 3 paragraph (11)`'s `the printed date of the issue` EQUALS (Date 2 8 2026)

-- Read fact for I2: SH 2463 item 12, printed in the same issue (30.7.2014) as the citing words of I2, amends section 41 by deleting words from it. Nothing more is recorded about it.
#ASSERT `SH 2463 item 12`'s `the printed date of the issue` EQUALS `item I2: section 113d(a)(1) cites section 41`'s `the printed date of the issue that prints the citing words`
#ASSERT `SH 2463 item 12`'s `the paragraphs of the Law it names` EQUALS LIST "41"
#ASSERT `the instrument names the paragraph` (TOSTRING (`item I2: section 113d(a)(1) cites section 41`'s `the number of the section cited`)) `SH 2463 item 12`
#ASSERT `SH 2463 item 12`'s `what the item does` EQUALS "deletes words from section 41"
#ASSERT `SH 2463 item 12`'s `the printed date of the issue` EQUALS (Date 30 7 2014)
